---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// TODO: replace href="#" with Amazon Associates links (OneLink) once account approved.
// TODO: Antonio to confirm final drive models.
---
<Base
  title="The DJ Emergency Kit - USB Drives That Don't Die | Save My Gig!"
  description="The USB drives actually worth trusting with your gig, chosen after 35 years around DJ booths. Max two recommendations per category, no filler."
  path="/gear"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">Approved_Gear</div>

    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1rem">THE EMERGENCY <span class="accent">KIT</span></h1>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:1rem">What I actually carry. Two options per category, never more, a wall of links means nobody chose anything.</p>
    <div class="review-flag">DRAFT - Antonio to confirm exact models. Affiliate links pending Amazon Associates approval.</div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">🔌 Main USB drives</h3>
      <p class="dim">32-64 GB is the sweet spot: big enough for a full working library, small enough that FAT32 formats without drama.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:1rem">SanDisk Extreme Pro USB 3.2</h3>
          <p>Metal body, fast, survives years of booth abuse. The default answer.</p>
          <a href="#" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="amazon" data-placement="gear_main_1">Check price →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:1rem">Samsung BAR Plus</h3>
          <p>Solid metal unibody, no cap to lose, quietly reliable.</p>
          <a href="#" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="amazon" data-placement="gear_main_2">Check price →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">🎒 The backup that lives in your pocket</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">Buy two of whichever main drive you pick. Identical drives, identical exports. That's the whole trick, redundancy beats recovery every time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">☔ Worth adding</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>A small hard case or keyring capsule, crushed and wet drives are half the lab jobs.</li>
        <li>A USB-C ↔ USB-A adapter, the booth laptop never has the port you need.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="dim" style="text-align:center;margin-top:2rem">
      Drive already failed? <a href="/recovery">Recovery route →</a> ·
      Full prevention system: <a href="/prepare">Never again →</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
